/**
  @page examples-io-medit MEDIT Format Conversion
  @brief Loading and converting meshes with MEDIT format

  @m_keywords{MEDIT, Mesh, Format Conversion}

  @tableofcontents

  @m_footernavigation

  @section examples-io-medit-intro Introduction

  This example demonstrates how to load a mesh in MEDIT format (commonly used
  with the [MMG](https://www.mmgtools.org/) remeshing tools) and save it in
  MFEM format.

  The MEDIT format (`.mesh`) is a text-based format developed at INRIA and is
  widely used in the French computational mechanics community.

  @section examples-io-medit-impl Implementation

  The implementation is straightforward — load in one format and save in
  another:

  @code{.cpp}
  #include <Rodin/Geometry.h>

  using namespace Rodin;
  using namespace Rodin::Geometry;

  int main(int, char** argv)
  {
    Mesh mesh;
    mesh.load(argv[1], IO::FileFormat::MEDIT);

    mesh.save("mfem.mesh", IO::FileFormat::MFEM);
  }
  @endcode

  @section examples-io-medit-usage Usage

  Run the example with a MEDIT mesh file as argument:

  @code{.bash}
  ./Rodin_IO_MEDIT input.mesh
  @endcode

  @section examples-io-medit-full Full Source Code

  The complete source code is:
  -   @ref IO/MEDIT.cpp "MEDIT.cpp"

  @section examples-io-medit-see-also See Also

  - @ref guides-io "I/O in Rodin"
  - @ref guides-io-meshformats "Mesh file formats"
  - @ref examples-mmg-index "MMG examples"

  @example IO/MEDIT.cpp @m_examplenavigation{examples-io-medit,IO/} @m_footernavigation
  */
